# Membership replacement domains

After K017's timeout, the two new candidate contracts partition the SAME query:
(a) scalar absence condition: for every i<22, n<=i or a[i]!=x;
(b) present witness: witness<n<=22 and a[witness]==x.
All unused cells remain arbitrary. The intended Lean domain law is finite-list
membership versus nonmembership on a.take n; present iff a witness exists.
Only after that law and BOTH native contract directions plus matched controls
may a caller use the partition. No source-level `.contains` result is a
precondition, and no conclusion/equality is assumed to prove itself.

Separate independent member: NHB_cursor_read_frame binds the same copied digest
block to query_words and ONE arbitrary iterator-next observation. It includes
cursor8 exhaustion. Its control changes exactly copied byte0. It does not
establish membership, survivor updates, caller loop induction or physical
chronological digest trace association.
